    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 1912 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution">Xinhai Revolution</a>, it ended more than two thousand years of imperial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>’s Nationalists it reunified much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 1928 and resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 1937 to 1945.</li><li>After losing the civil war in 1949 it moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>, where martial-law rule gave way to democracy in the 1990s.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> was a founding member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> and held one of the five permanent seats on the Security Council until 1971.</p></aside>
    </section>

